+\paragraph{Core-scale no-go audit.}
+For non-overlapping tubes of radius $r_c$ with occupied fraction
+$0<\varphi_v\le1$,
+\begin{align}
+    \mathcal L_v
+    =
+    \frac{\varphi_v}{\pi r_c^2},
+    \qquad
+    \eta_A^{\rm SST}
+    =
+    \frac{\varphi_v\ln q}{2\pi r_c^2}.
+\end{align}
+The strongest minimal binary model, $\varphi_v=1$ and $q=2$, gives
+\begin{align}
+    \eta_{A,\max}^{(r_c,q=2)}
+    =
+    5.557020457583\times10^{28}\,\mathrm{m^{-2}}.
+\end{align}
+Only as an external post-derivation comparison, the observed $G$ corresponds
+to
+\begin{align}
+    \eta_A^{\rm GR}
+    =
+    \frac{c^3}{4\hbar G}
+    =
+    9.570182792895\times10^{68}\,\mathrm{m^{-2}},
+\end{align}
+so
+\begin{align}
+    \boxed{
+    \frac{\eta_A^{\rm GR}}
+    {\eta_{A,\max}^{(r_c,q=2)}}
+    =
+    1.722178794544\times10^{40}
+    }.
+\end{align}
+Thus independent binary $r_c$-scale piercings are rejected as a complete
+explanation of the gravitational area coefficient. Promotion requires an
+independent derivation of $\mathcal L_v$, $q$, piercing correlations, and the
+reversible channel-activation dynamics, together with a non-ad-hoc resolution
+of this area-density deficit.
